---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '@/components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '@/components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SupportingPage from '@/components/SupportingPage.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About SpellingWords | K–5 Spelling Practice"
  description="Learn what SpellingWords is, who it serves, and how its focused K–5 spelling curriculum, reference pages, and practice tools work together."
>
  <SiteHeader currentPath="/about" />
  <SupportingPage
    eyebrow="About the site"
    title="About SpellingWords"
    intro="SpellingWords.app is a focused K–5 spelling website for students, parents, and teachers. It brings together structured grade-level curriculum, clear spelling references, and calm interactive practice."
    currentPath="/about"
  >
    <section aria-labelledby="why-heading">
      <h2 id="why-heading">A place to focus on spelling</h2>
      <p>
        Spelling deserves a learning space of its own. SpellingWords helps children hear a word,
        think through its letters and patterns, type it, and check their work without timers,
        points, streaks, or a crowded game interface.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is intentionally not a general literacy platform. It does not try to replace
        reading instruction, writing instruction, or a school curriculum. Its job is narrower: to
        make useful K–5 spelling knowledge easier to find, understand, and practice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="paths-heading">
      <h2 id="paths-heading">Three ways to use SpellingWords</h2>
      <div class="supporting-cards">
        <div class="supporting-card">
          <h3>Practice your own words</h3>
          <p>
            Enter a school list or any words that need attention and begin a focused practice
            session.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/practice-your-own-words">Start with your words</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="supporting-card">
          <h3>Follow a grade</h3>
          <p>
            Browse Kindergarten through 5th Grade to find an organized spelling path for each year.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/#grades">Browse all grades</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="supporting-card">
          <h3>Look up a skill</h3>
          <p>
            Use grade-independent references when a child needs help with one particular spelling
            pattern.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/skills">Browse spelling skills</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="audience-heading">
      <h2 id="audience-heading">Built for students and the adults who support them</h2>
      <p>
        Students can practice in a quiet interface with clear feedback. Parents can find an
        appropriate starting point without needing specialist terminology. Teachers and homeschool
        educators can use the grade and Skill architecture as a supplemental source of focused
        practice.
      </p>
      <p>
        No account or login is required. That keeps the path from choosing words to practicing them
        short, especially when a child is using a shared or classroom device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="method-heading">
      <h2 id="method-heading">A spelling-specific curriculum</h2>
      <p>
        The curriculum is organized around spelling patterns, high-frequency words, meaningful
        grade-level progression, and selected themed practice. Educational usefulness matters more
        than publishing the largest possible collection of word pages.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read <a href="/curriculum">Our Spelling Curriculum</a> for the full parent- and teacher-friendly
        explanation of how the paths are organized and how content earns a place on the site.
      </p>
    </section>
  </SupportingPage>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
